  short="Typhoid is an infection spread through contaminated food and water. It causes fever that rises over several days, headache, belly pain, weakness and loose motions or constipation. A blood culture, not the Widal test, is the reliable test. It needs a full course of the right antibiotic, prescribed by a doctor. A vaccine is available.",
